WEBVTT

NOTE editing-station-targets: written VO text from episode.json, timed from the timeline VO placements

V0-1
00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:05.930
Change one station's target, and
watch what it does to the suggestion.

V1a-1
00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:16.883
The table drills from course to
areas, then holes, then stations.

V1a-2
00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:20.280
Breadcrumbs at the top left
take you back up a level.

V1b-1
00:00:22.306 --> 00:00:25.471
If you already know where the
station is, click it on the map:

V1b-2
00:00:25.571 --> 00:00:28.686
the table drills straight to
its hole and scrolls to the row.

V2a-1
00:00:35.183 --> 00:00:39.553
The Target VWC field takes a
whole number between 0 and 50.

V2b-1
00:00:41.916 --> 00:00:45.676
Raising it increases the deficit
and therefore the suggestion;

V2b-2
00:00:45.776 --> 00:00:47.596
lowering it does the opposite.

V3a-1
00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:56.990
The Suggested column recalculates
against the new target.

V3b-1
00:00:59.323 --> 00:01:02.039
If it lands on the highest
value in the column,

V3b-2
00:01:02.139 --> 00:01:06.013
the daily maximum is capping it
rather than the target deciding it.

V4a-1
00:01:13.826 --> 00:01:18.676
The % Adj. field is separate from the
target and accepts 0 to 900. Override

V4a-2
00:01:18.776 --> 00:01:23.756
it when the suggestion looks too high
or too low for a station you know well.

V4b-1
00:01:25.010 --> 00:01:28.289
Editing it queues the station
for push when the station is

V4b-2
00:01:28.389 --> 00:01:32.064
enabled and the new value differs
from the Current value in Lynx.

V4b-3
00:01:32.164 --> 00:01:35.500
The Suggested value stays
visible beside it for comparison.
